    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2021-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\log_{40}2}=\\log_2 40\\) and \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\log_{20}2}=\\log_2 20,\\) the expression becomes \\((\\log_2 80)(\\log_2 40)\\) \\(-(\\log_2 160)(\\log_2 20).\\)\n\nLet \\(t=\\log_2 5.\\) Then \\(\\log_2 80=4+t,\\) \\(\\log_2 40=3+t,\\) \\(\\log_2 160=5+t,\\) \\(\\log_2 20=2+t.\\)\n\nThe value is \\((4+t)(3+t)\\) \\(-(5+t)(2+t)\\) \\(=(12+7t+t^2)\\) \\(-(10+7t+t^2)\\) \\(=2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(\\dfrac{1}{\\log_{40}2}=\\log_2 40,\\) and similarly for the other reciprocal",
        "Write everything in terms of \\(t=\\log_2 5,\\) since \\(\\log_2 80=4+t,\\) etc."
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
